  <prompt>
    Author the automated ProseMirror test that proves Success Criterion 3 (AI drift-proof). Two behaviors,
    both under real editor state:
    (1) GENERATION WITH CONCURRENT EDITS lands at the REBASED selection — drop the generate-window bookmark
        (task 040), simulate concurrent user edits during the request window, let the AI return paraId-anchored
        operations, and assert the operations land at the rebased selection (bookmark resolved to its current
        position), NOT the stale original offset.
    (2) A BAD/OUT-OF-RANGE anchor is REFUSED — feed a returned operation with an unknown paraId / out-of-range
        offset and assert it is surfaced (as a review comment), NOT placed (task 041 validation gate).

    Tests live under `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/`. Exercise real ProseMirror/TipTap
    editor state — NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests (ADR-038). This is
    the automated evidence for Success Criterion 3 (the other evidence is CIPO operator UAT in Phase 6).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript test engineer fluent in TipTap 3 / ProseMirror test harnessing (constructing a
    real editor state, dispatching transactions to simulate concurrent edits, asserting resolved positions and
    marks). Understands the two behaviors under proof are the rebased-selection landing and the refused-bad-anchor.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A green automated ProseMirror test suite that proves: generation with concurrent user edits lands at the
    rebased selection; and a bad/out-of-range anchor is refused (surfaced, not placed). `npm run build:prod`
    for the shared lib is green.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Success Criterion 3 (spec + design §10): "AI drift-proof — generation with concurrent edits lands at the
      rebased selection; bad anchors refused. Verify: automated ProseMirror test + UAT on CIPO." This task is
      the automated ProseMirror test half. It exercises the capture (040 bookmark + resolve-on-return) and apply
      (041 validate + refuse) paths end-to-end in the editor without hitting the network — the AI return is
      simulated as paraId-anchored operations (and, for the negative case, a bad anchor).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/aiAnchoring.test.ts — NEW ProseMirror test: rebased-selection landing + refused-bad-anchor</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useAiGenerateBookmark.ts — task 040/041 bookmark + validate-before-apply gate under test</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts — the schema carrying `data-paraid`; build the test editor state with paraIds</file>
      <file role="reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/ — existing Vitest/ProseMirror test setup to mirror</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §10 (Success Criterion 3)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md Success Criterion 3, FR-07</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="040" status="pending">Generate-window bookmark + resolve-on-return (the capture path under test).</dependency>
      <dependency task="041" status="pending">Validate-before-apply gate + fuzzy-as-comment fallback (the refuse-bad-anchor path under test).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / Success Criterion 3">The test MUST prove BOTH: generation with concurrent edits lands at the rebased selection; AND a bad/out-of-range anchor is refused (surfaced, not placed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Tests exercise REAL ProseMirror/TipTap editor state (construct editor, dispatch transactions to simulate concurrent edits). NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests. The AI return is simulated as paraId-anchored operations — no live network.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / project">Include an ADR-021 dark-mode render assertion on any surfaced review-comment UI produced in the refuse-bad-anchor case.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / project">Test harness uses the MIT ProseMirror/TipTap base only — no `@tiptap-pro/*`, no AGPL, no EigenPal dependency.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ProseMirror/TipTap test harnessing; simulating concurrent edits via transactions; asserting resolved positions + surfaced comments; Vitest</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Real-editor-state test" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/">
        Mirror the existing Vitest/ProseMirror setup: build a real editor with paraId'd paragraphs, dispatch transactions to simulate concurrent edits, and assert resolved positions/marks — no mocked transport.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor (TEST-MODIFYING override — code-review + adr-check unconditionally). Load ADR-038 + the existing test setup + the 040/041 hooks under test.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Rebased-selection test">Construct a real editor with paraId'd paragraphs; select a phrase; drop the generate-window bookmark (040); dispatch transactions simulating concurrent user edits during the request window; feed a simulated AI return of paraId-anchored operations; assert the operations land at the REBASED selection (resolved bookmark position), not the stale original offset.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Refused-bad-anchor test">Feed a simulated AI return with an unknown paraId / out-of-range offset; assert the op is REFUSED and surfaced as a review comment (041 gate), and the document text at that location is unchanged.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Dark-mode assertion">Assert the surfaced review-comment UI renders under the Fluent v9 dark theme (ADR-021).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify + index">Run the tests (green) and `npm run build:prod` (green). Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>No automated test exists for AI generation landing at the rebased selection under concurrent edits.</existing>
    <extension>No — this is the test for the new AI-anchoring surface (040/041).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Success Criterion 3 (AI drift-proof) has no regression guard; the generate-window drift defect could silently return.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/aiAnchoring.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A ProseMirror test proves generation with CONCURRENT user edits lands at the REBASED selection (bookmark resolved to current position), not the stale original offset — GREEN.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A ProseMirror test proves a bad/out-of-range anchor is REFUSED and surfaced (not placed); the document text at that location is unchanged — GREEN.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE case covered: the refused-anchor test asserts NO silent placement occurred at any location.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests exercise real ProseMirror/TipTap editor state (no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;` / DI / ctor-null; no live network); no `@tiptap-pro/*` / AGPL / EigenPal dependency.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Surfaced review-comment UI renders correctly in Fluent v9 dark mode (ADR-021); shared-lib `npm run build:prod` is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Generation with concurrent edits lands at rebased selection">
      <steps>Real editor; select phrase; drop bookmark; dispatch concurrent-edit transactions; feed paraId-anchored AI operations.</steps>
      <expected>Operations land at the rebased selection; assertion on resolved position passes.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Bad anchor is refused, not placed">
      <steps>Feed an operation with an unknown paraId / out-of-range offset.</steps>
      <expected>Op is surfaced as a review comment; no text mutation at that location; no silent placement anywhere.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render the surfaced review-comment UI under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>UI uses theme tokens and is legible in dark mode; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    Automated evidence for Success Criterion 3; the complementary evidence is CIPO operator UAT (task 062).
    No BFF surface changes here (client tests only), so no seam slice required for this task.

    ── COMPLETION (2026-07-22) ──
    NEW test file: src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/aiAnchoring.test.tsx
    (9 tests). DEVIATION from the POML-listed `.ts` extension: named `.tsx` because the ADR-021 dark-mode
    assertion renders `ComposeAiToolbar` via RTL, which requires JSX (a `.ts` file cannot contain JSX) —
    documented here per the "state any deviation" step; not a scope or behavior change.

    Deliberately did NOT duplicate what 040/041's own suites already prove:
      - 040's `useAiGenerateBookmark.test.tsx` already asserts the BOOKMARK rebases through a concurrent
        edit (position-level assertions) and (041 addition) that an 'operations' result reaches
        `aiApplyValidation.validateAndApply`, plus a generic hand-built-item dark-mode render.
      - 041's `useAiApplyValidation.test.ts` already proves the pure validator/applier/fuzzy-fallback unit
        behavior in isolation, including the AUTO-band-never-auto-applies escalation guard.
    This file adds the CROSS-CUTTING, END-TO-END proof Success Criterion 3 names: (1) a REAL concurrent
    edit + a simulated AI-returned op anchored at the REBASED bookmark point lands on the actually-moved
    text — asserted against the resulting DOCUMENT TEXT ("PREFIX The quick swift fox…"), not just a
    resolved position, plus a CONTRAST test showing the stale (un-rebased) offset would have pointed at
    the wrong text; (2) an unknown-paraId AND an out-of-range-offset case both refused end-to-end through
    040+041 together (not applied, surfaced, document text unchanged — the NEGATIVE "no silent placement
    anywhere" proof); (3) a dark-mode render of the review UI produced by a REAL `useAiApplyValidation`
    controller's own output (not a stub), via a small `RefusedAnchorHost` test component.

    Verify: `npx jest aiAnchoring` → 9/9 pass. `npm run typecheck` — R4 files clean (same pre-existing
    `@spaarke/*` sibling-dist environmental errors as 040/041; unrelated). No escalation.
  </notes>

